+## Hybrid procedural infinite world (added 2026-05-10)
+
+Direction captured in conversation: use the real OpenTopo data we
+already have to *inform* procedural generation, not as something to
+stretch into infinity. Real DEMs serve two roles — hero zones at
+runtime and reference/training data for procedural extraction.
+
+Approach is classical, not neural: per-biome spectral fitting from
+the cached corpus, Landlab fluvial+diffusion erosion as the
+visual-quality backbone, real-DEM patch seeding as the close-play
+quality lift, and a streaming director that decides per-chunk
+whether to serve cached source-stack data, pre-baked procedural
+neighbors, or on-demand patch-seeded synthesis. Style packs
+(photoreal / painterly / topographic) ride on top via the existing
+per-mode `.tres` swap — same height/splat, different shaders and
+materials.
+
+Realistic end-state: current source-stack scene quality, infinite,
+with believable biome transitions. Procedural zones at ~85-90% of
+cached-region quality across walk close/medium and iso/topdown.
+**Not** Google-Earth quality; the corpus and the workflows we have
+do not support that bar and we do not pretend otherwise.
+
+Composes with M1-M18 infrastructure: material catalog, splat
+shader, M2/M7 transitions, M10 seam integration, M11 junctions, M12
+view-mode parity, M5/M6 streaming + source-stack contract, M14
+texture bakeoff, M15 scatter, M16 gallery, and M17 procedural
+neighbor extraction. Only new dependency is Landlab.
+
+Plan in `world3/docs/M19_M24_HYBRID_PROCEDURAL_ROADMAP_2026_05_10.md`.
+Gated by M13-M18 closure + at least one accepted M17 procedural
+neighbor bake. Pre-work (corpus feasibility spike, Landlab API
+skim, biome coverage gap analysis) can start any time without
+violating the gate.
